With less than six months to go before the presidential election, the 11 November commemorations have taken on a political hue. On Wednesday, Emmanuel Macron presided over his final ceremony in Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e1342ca-dde8-11f1-8f2e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T144944Z-1574455219-RC2OLOAGKZUY-RTRMADP-3-REMEMBRANCE-DAY-FRANCE-MACRON.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e1342ca-dde8-11f1-8f2e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T144944Z-1574455219-RC2OLOAGKZUY-RTRMADP-3-REMEMBRANCE-DAY-FRANCE-MACRON.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56426a08-dde7-11f1-8754-0597623c4bd3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:57:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain: General strike over housing costs before national election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election</link><description>
Millions of Spanish workers shut down businesses and public transportation in a protest on Wednesday over housing costs that the government hopes to leverage before a national election later this month. The walkout — under the slogan “Salaries. Housing. Prices.” — was the first general strike in Spain in 14 years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2694a56-dde7-11f1-b92c-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T135107Z-1475091229-RC2OLOAL1V8D-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-STRIKE-MADRID-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2694a56-dde7-11f1-b92c-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T135107Z-1475091229-RC2OLOAL1V8D-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-STRIKE-MADRID-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60153f8a-dde5-11f1-a6a9-2ba289beda67</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:54:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Exclusive: EU's Kallas says US 'can't negotiate on our behalf' on lifting Russia sanctions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions</link><description>
In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, the EU's top diplomat Kaja Kallas discusses the war in Ukraine, the situation in the Middle East and a possible change in US President Donald Trump's foreign policy following the US midterm elections. The former Estonian prime minister, who is now the European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, also reaffirms the EU's position as a major player on the global geopolitical stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f35d22fe-dd08-11f1-828d-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-KAJA-KALLAS.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f35d22fe-dd08-11f1-828d-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-KAJA-KALLAS.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a313c31e-dd0a-11f1-b029-e510b4906617</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:15:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Caroline DE CAMARET</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Charlotte Gainsbourg brings pioneering French lawyer Gisèle Halimi to the screen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261111-charlotte-gainsbourg-brings-pioneering-french-lawyer-gis%C3%A8le-halimi-to-the-screen</link><description>
